        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(active-memory): bound timeout circuit breakers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Active Memory's process-local `timeoutCircuitBreaker` map could grow without bound: entries were only removed when the same key was checked after cooldown or after a later success, so distinct failing agent/provider/model combinations that were never revisited stayed for the process lifetime.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBound the map on its owner mutation path (`recordCircuitBreakerTimeout`): purge cooldown-expired entries using the normalized configured `circuitBreakerCooldownMs`, then evict oldest `lastTimeoutAt` until under `DEFAULT_MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES` (1000) before inserting a new key. Updating an existing key refreshes counters/time and purges expired peers without evicting the active key.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** Each new failing agent/provider/model pair could permanently add process state; purge ignored non-default cooldowns.\n**After:** Peer purge honors configured cooldown (5s–600s); remaining breaker state has a hard cap of 1000 keys.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Base: `4289c6c16cd5` / Head: `e5f35dad40`\n- Node: v24.18.0 / Windows\n- Production Map proof (`node --import tsx` on `recordCircuitBreakerTimeout`): insert 1005 → size 1000, oldest evicted, newest kept\n- Focused vitest for cooldown purge + bound + runtime hook path green\n- CI: `check-test-types` fixed for the runtime-proof test\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed:** Live gateway Active Memory recall timeouts record distinct agent keys; a follow-up turn within cooldown skips recall with `circuit breaker open`.\n**Environment tested:** Windows, Node v24.18.0, worktree `codex/active-memory-bound-timeout-breakers`, real gateway child process with `plugins.slots.memory=memory-core` and `plugins.entries.active-memory` enabled; webchat Control UI client; hang recall provider (TCP accept, no HTTP response); fail-fast main provider (HTTP 401).\n**Steps run after the patch:**\n1. Start ephemeral gateway with agents `am0`/`am1`/`am2`, `timeoutMs=800`, `circuitBreakerMaxTimeouts=1`, `circuitBreakerCooldownMs=600000`, `logging=true`.\n2. Send webchat `chat.send` for each agent (distinct timeout keys).\n3. Immediately re-send for `am0` within cooldown.\n**Evidence after fix:**\n\n```text\n[plugins] active-memory: agent=am0 session=<redacted> activeProvider=hang activeModel=slow done status=timeout elapsedMs=2566 summaryChars=0\n[plugins] active-memory: agent=am1 session=<redacted> activeProvider=hang activeModel=slow done status=timeout elapsedMs=4855 summaryChars=0\n[plugins] active-memory: agent=am2 session=<redacted> activeProvider=hang activeModel=slow done status=timeout elapsedMs=4844 summaryChars=0\n[plugins] active-memory: agent=am0 session=<redacted> activeProvider=hang activeModel=slow skipped (circuit breaker open after consecutive timeouts)\n```\n\nAlso observed gateway ready line listing both `active-memory` and `memory-core` among loaded plugins.\n**Observed result:** `timeoutLogCount=3`, `breakerSkipLogCount=1` on the live gateway path.\n**Not tested:** 1000-key cap soak under multi-hour live gateway load (covered by production Map unit/production-function proof).\n",
